precept BillOfMaterialsManagement

# A manufacturing engineer builds out the bill of materials for a finished
# product over time — adding components and their per-assembly quantities,
# referencing sub-assemblies, and assigning a revision letter. Once the BOM is
# complete it goes through engineering review, gets released to production
# (Active), and eventually is superseded by a newer revision (Replaced) or
# retired without successor (Obsolete).
#
# Free-Construction: the engineer enriches a Draft over time. Required-at-
# release fields are declared optional and gated by the Submit event's ensures.
# Components are modeled as a parallel pair — ComponentPartNumbers (set) for
# membership tests, Components (lookup) for per-part quantities. The set is
# the source of truth for membership; the lookup carries quantity. The two are
# kept consistent by the AddComponent/UpdateComponentQuantity/RemoveComponent
# rows. This mirrors the canonical shopping-cart pattern.

# Identity and ownership
field BomId as string optional maxlength 50
field ProductCode as string optional maxlength 50
field ProductDescription as string optional maxlength 200
field Revision as string optional maxlength 10
field EngineerName as string optional maxlength 100

# Effective dating
field EffectiveFrom as date optional
field EffectiveTo as date optional

# Components — distinct part numbers (set, for membership testing) and the
# per-assembly quantity required (lookup, for value lookup). Kept consistent
# by the component transition rows. TotalComponentUnits accumulates units across
# all components so guards can reason about BOM size without iterating.
field ComponentPartNumbers as set of string
field Components as lookup of string to integer
field TotalComponentUnits as integer default 0 nonnegative

# Sub-assembly references — a separate set of child-BOM IDs this BOM depends on.
field SubAssemblies as set of string

# Approval and supersession audit
field ApproverName as string optional maxlength 100
field SupersededByBomId as string optional maxlength 50
field ObsoleteReason as string optional
field ChangeLog as log of string

# Timestamps
field SubmittedAt as instant optional
field ApprovedAt as instant optional
field ActivatedAt as instant optional
field ReplacedAt as instant optional
field ObsoletedAt as instant optional

# Rules
rule EffectiveTo > EffectiveFrom when EffectiveFrom is set and EffectiveTo is set because "Effective end {EffectiveTo} must be after effective start {EffectiveFrom}"
rule TotalComponentUnits >= ComponentPartNumbers.count because "Total component units ({TotalComponentUnits}) cannot be less than distinct component count ({ComponentPartNumbers.count}) — every component contributes at least one unit"

# States
state Draft initial
state UnderReview
state Approved
state Active
state Replaced terminal
state Obsolete terminal

# State ensures
in UnderReview ensure SubmittedAt is set because "A BOM under review must carry a submission timestamp"
in Approved ensure ApproverName is set because "An approved BOM must record the approver"
in Approved ensure ApprovedAt is set because "An approved BOM must carry an approval timestamp"
in Active ensure ActivatedAt is set because "An active BOM must record when it was released to production"
in Active ensure EffectiveFrom is set because "An active BOM must have an effective-from date on file"
in Replaced ensure SupersededByBomId is set because "Replaced BOMs must reference their successor"
in Obsolete ensure ObsoleteReason is set because "Obsoleted BOMs must record a retirement reason"

# Editable windows — full planning in Draft; engineer can correct metadata while
# the BOM is still under review (e.g., to address review feedback).
in Draft modify BomId, ProductCode, ProductDescription, Revision, EngineerName, EffectiveFrom, EffectiveTo editable
in UnderReview modify ProductDescription, EffectiveFrom, EffectiveTo editable

# Events
event AddComponent(PartNumber as string notempty, Quantity as integer positive)
event UpdateComponentQuantity(PartNumber as string notempty, NewQuantity as integer positive)
event RemoveComponent(PartNumber as string notempty)
event AddSubAssembly(SubBomId as string notempty)
event RemoveSubAssembly(SubBomId as string notempty)
event Submit
event Approve(Approver as string notempty)
event RequestRevisions(Reason as string notempty)
event Activate
event Supersede(SuccessorBomId as string notempty)
event Obsolete(Reason as string notempty)

on Submit ensure BomId is set because "BOM ID is required before submission"
on Submit ensure ProductCode is set because "Product code is required before submission"
on Submit ensure ProductDescription is set because "Product description is required before submission"
on Submit ensure Revision is set because "Revision letter is required before submission"
on Submit ensure EngineerName is set because "Owning engineer must be on record before submission"
on Submit ensure EffectiveFrom is set because "Effective-from date is required before submission"

# Transitions

# Draft component management — add, update, remove.
# A duplicate add is rejected — the engineer should use UpdateComponentQuantity
# instead so the audit trail captures the change as an update, not a re-add.
from Draft on AddComponent when ComponentPartNumbers contains AddComponent.PartNumber
    -> reject "Component {AddComponent.PartNumber} already in BOM — use UpdateComponentQuantity to change its quantity"
from Draft on AddComponent
    -> add ComponentPartNumbers AddComponent.PartNumber
    -> put Components AddComponent.PartNumber = AddComponent.Quantity
    -> set TotalComponentUnits = TotalComponentUnits + AddComponent.Quantity
    -> append ChangeLog AddComponent.PartNumber
    -> no transition

from Draft on UpdateComponentQuantity when ComponentPartNumbers contains UpdateComponentQuantity.PartNumber
    -> set TotalComponentUnits = TotalComponentUnits - (Components for UpdateComponentQuantity.PartNumber) + UpdateComponentQuantity.NewQuantity
    -> put Components UpdateComponentQuantity.PartNumber = UpdateComponentQuantity.NewQuantity
    -> append ChangeLog UpdateComponentQuantity.PartNumber
    -> no transition
from Draft on UpdateComponentQuantity
    -> reject "Component {UpdateComponentQuantity.PartNumber} not in BOM — use AddComponent to add it"

# Remove a component: drop membership from the set and the lookup entry.
from Draft on RemoveComponent when ComponentPartNumbers contains RemoveComponent.PartNumber
    -> set TotalComponentUnits = TotalComponentUnits - (Components for RemoveComponent.PartNumber)
    -> remove Components RemoveComponent.PartNumber
    -> remove ComponentPartNumbers RemoveComponent.PartNumber
    -> append ChangeLog RemoveComponent.PartNumber
    -> no transition
from Draft on RemoveComponent
    -> reject "Component {RemoveComponent.PartNumber} not in BOM — nothing to remove"

# Sub-assembly references — a BOM can depend on other BOMs as sub-assemblies.
from Draft on AddSubAssembly when SubAssemblies contains AddSubAssembly.SubBomId
    -> reject "Sub-assembly {AddSubAssembly.SubBomId} already referenced"
from Draft on AddSubAssembly when AddSubAssembly.SubBomId == BomId
    -> reject "A BOM cannot reference itself as a sub-assembly"
from Draft on AddSubAssembly
    -> add SubAssemblies AddSubAssembly.SubBomId
    -> append ChangeLog AddSubAssembly.SubBomId
    -> no transition

from Draft on RemoveSubAssembly when SubAssemblies contains RemoveSubAssembly.SubBomId
    -> remove SubAssemblies RemoveSubAssembly.SubBomId
    -> append ChangeLog RemoveSubAssembly.SubBomId
    -> no transition
from Draft on RemoveSubAssembly
    -> reject "Sub-assembly {RemoveSubAssembly.SubBomId} not referenced — nothing to remove"

# Submission — requires at least one component so the BOM is meaningful.
from Draft on Submit when ComponentPartNumbers.count == 0
    -> reject "Cannot submit an empty BOM — add at least one component first"
from Draft on Submit
    -> set SubmittedAt = now()
    -> transition UnderReview

# Approval and request-for-revisions
from UnderReview on Approve
    -> set ApproverName = Approve.Approver
    -> set ApprovedAt = now()
    -> transition Approved

from UnderReview on RequestRevisions
    -> append ChangeLog RequestRevisions.Reason
    -> transition Draft

# Activation — the BOM is released to production.
from Approved on Activate
    -> set ActivatedAt = now()
    -> transition Active

# Supersession — a successor BOM (typically a new revision) takes over.
from Active on Supersede
    -> set SupersededByBomId = Supersede.SuccessorBomId
    -> set ReplacedAt = now()
    -> transition Replaced

# Obsolescence — the product is retired with no successor.
from Active on Obsolete
    -> set ObsoleteReason = Obsolete.Reason
    -> set ObsoletedAt = now()
    -> transition Obsolete
